# Testing

- Any new function in `lib/permissions/` MUST ship with a test covering:
  the happy path, missing role, wrong tenant, and (if applicable) missing
  DataGrant. These four cases are the minimum, not a suggestion.
- API routes get at least one integration test per HTTP status they can
  return (200, 401, 403, 404, 422).
- Use React Testing Library for components — test behavior (what the user
  sees/does), not implementation details (internal state, class names).
- Don't mock the permission-check layer in integration tests for
  security-sensitive routes — that's the exact thing being tested.
- Snapshot tests are discouraged for anything with dynamic dates/prices.
